These are needed that the dhcpd replies.
He does not see a request.
This may be because SRM has problems with the interface or because
of LAN problems between the client and dhcp server.
I've seen failures with suns because the switchnetwork need to long
establish the path when an interface goes up.
The suns hadn't tried long enough.
Maybe there are similar issues with SRM.
You can usually handle this by configuring you switches acordingly.

