On Sat, Apr 13, 2002 at 08:47:23PM +0200, Riccardo.Veraldi@fi.infn.it wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> today I saw this message from my kernel
> 
> Apr 12 15:00:02 durlindana /kernel: Warning: received processor correctable error.
> 
> What it could be ??
> I have a Miata running FreeBSD 4.5-stable

A processessor correctable error is an error condition fixed by
hardware or PALcode.
Most likely it's an ECC error on RAM.

DRAM has a softerror rate so single bit errors ocur every now and then.
If you get less than once a month I wouldn't worry about.

