I'd hold on with that for a moment... I was able to gather 14 different
ISA NICs for testing with FreeBSD alpha. However, I was only able to get
the kernel to recognize 3 of them, all of which were different models
of 3com EtherLink III.

With small modifications to files, files.i386, options and options.i386 I
was able to compile these drivers into the kernel: cs, ep, ex, fe, le, sn.

These would not compile: ed, lnc, sbni.

Now I admit that due to time constraints, all I did was put a card in,
boot the system and see if the card was recognized by kernel. If not, I
moved on.

