I'm very keen to fix this. Firstly, what is a PC164SX? (The headers
suggest that it is some kind of Alpha).

Can you put the 'device random' back in, and try turning off entropy
harvesting by turning off each of the following sysctls to see if any
of them "fix" the problem?

kern.random.sys.harvest.ethernet
kern.random.sys.harvest.point_to_point
kern.random.sys.harvest.interrupt

I am suspecting that a high-rate interrupt is being harvested, and
that this is the problem.

Also, please run 'systat 2 -vmstat' for a while, and stare at the irqs
(top-right-ish) and see if any/which of them are high-rate interrupt
sources, and let me know which.

Is it possible to get an account on this box?

